    {"Redundant leading ``bash``/``sh`` invocations are unwrapped for Git Bash.\012\012    Agents commonly emit ``bash cd /c/dev/x && ...`` or ``bash -c '...'`` as a\012    habit; the Bash tool already runs the whole string via bash, so keeping the\012    wrapper makes bash try to open ``cd`` (or the inline script) as a script\012    file and fail on Windows.  The scanner removes the redundant wrapper and,\012    for the ``-c`` form, scans the inline script so fallback commands and\012    Windows paths inside it are fixed too.\012    ", "", "/c/dev/x", "", "", "", "Redundant leading ``bash``/``sh`` invocations are unwrapped for Git Bash.\012\012    Agents commonly emit ``bash cd C:/dev/x && ...`` or ``bash -c '...'`` as a\012    habit; the Bash tool already runs the whole string via bash, so keeping the\012    wrapper makes bash try to open ``cd`` (or the inline script) as a script\012    file and fail on Windows.  The scanner removes the redundant wrapper and,\012    for the ``-c`` form, scans the inline script so fallback commands and\012    Windows paths inside it are fixed too.\012    ", "Rewrote Windows path(s) for Git Bash (backslashes to forward slashes; Git Bash virtual paths to native spellings): `/c/dev/x`."},
