    {"Repair a heredoc terminator followed by a control operator.\012\012    Bash requires a control operator that continues a heredoc-delimited command\012    to appear on the same line as the ``<<`` redirection.  A common model\012    mistake is to place ``&&`` (or ``||``, ``;``, ``|``...) on the line after\012    the closing delimiter, which produces ``syntax error near unexpected token\012    `&&'``.  The fixer moves the operator (and the command it chains) to the\012    redirection line, leaving the heredoc body and delimiter untouched.\012    ", "", "", "", "", "", "Repair a heredoc terminator followed by a control operator.\012\012    Bash requires a control operator that continues a heredoc-delimited command\012    to appear on the same line as the ``<<`` redirection.  A common model\012    mistake is to place ``&&`` (or ``||``, ``;``, ``|``...) on the line after\012    the closing delimiter, which produces ``syntax error near unexpected token\012    `&&'``.  The fixer moves the operator (and the command it chains) to the\012    redirection line, leaving the heredoc body and delimiter untouched.\012    ", ""},
